    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c38cd172",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a person holding a rifle-like object, aiming it out of a window, with text overlay that reads 'when the new call of duty comes out and you're already camping.' The overall intent is to humorously convey the frustration or anticipation of a gamer who is already deeply immersed in a game (specifically 'camping'—a term used in gaming to describe staying in one place to ambush opponents) when a new installment of 'Call of Duty' is released. The meme uses the visual of aiming a weapon to symbolize the gamer's readiness and eagerness to play the new game. There is no toxicity present in this meme; it is a lighthearted, self-referential joke targeting gamers and their habits, not any protected group or community. The intent is to create relatable humor through analogical mapping: the act of aiming a weapon (visual) is mapped to the gamer's intense focus and readiness to play (textual), highlighting the common experience of being 'camped out' in gaming culture.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_fbb531bb"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
